1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a certain day
drifting on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes fly off too.

3
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:32,960
Onto the head of the carpenter
who was saving his money,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I've left some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pachinko, savings,
one more yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape feels oddly gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed-hat water spout,

9
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset sinks into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness lost again...

12
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,480
I only realized it after listening,
because I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:55,880
Right, most camper vans are American-made,
since that's where they originated.

14
00:01:55,880 --> 00:02:04,940
There are all kinds, but this one is completely a house!
That's called a mobile home. It has wheels underneath, so it can be moved.

15
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:14,480
Dragging your whole house along to go camping... more like a rich man's indulgence, isn't it?
That crane, wasn't it the Porsche from Shiratori 0 o'clock?

16
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,060
Listen up, you poor folks.

17
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:21,520
Long time no see.

18
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:23,260
What the heck is this?

19
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:25,640
As you can see, it's a camper van.

20
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,220
It's the very epitome of
a nouveau riche mindset.

21
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:31,820
There's only one like it in the world,
made for the super-rich Seatley Rage.

22
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:35,300
Is a custom-made Porsche
camper really that rare?

23
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:38,160
It goes beyond the word "rare."

24
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,800
Don't praise me so much.

25
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,760
I'm not praising you!

26
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:41,600
I feel great.

27
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:43,080
Just a greeting.

28
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,880
Falling for the same trick every time

29
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,500
Figures it's just more
kids' bank notes again.

30
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,700
Ryo-chan!

31
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,500
These are real, senpai.

32
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:00,580
Didn't you say super-rich
people only carry cards?

33
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:04,320
Don't think of me as
just some super-rich guy.

34
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:08,680
Because you may have forgotten, but

35
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:12,500
Last time,
I had trouble paying just 25 yen by card.

36
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:15,560
So from now on, I've decided to carry both.

37
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:19,620
In other words, I'm a super-rich
man who learns from his mistakes.

38
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,160
Doesn't that mean it's
finally become normal?

39
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,340
Look who's talking!

40
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:28,960
Japan still can't really be called
a fully cashless society, can it?

41
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:32,040
Whatever money you find,
you have to give it all back.

42
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,620
Hey, super-rich guy, that camper of yours...

43
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:40,900
The engine's an air-cooled six-cylinder
twin-turbo with 512 horsepower.

44
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:46,280
Looks like even the rich man himself understands
the value of this genuine Porsche camper.

45
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,880
Wasting money on such nonsense!

46
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,540
Ryo & Reiko?

47
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,740
How do you know my name?

48
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,780
That's for you, Reiko.

49
00:03:55,560 --> 00:04:00,520
It's a super-special camper custom-built
just so we can go auto camping together.

50
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:06,400
Come on, Reiko,
take the first step into our super camper.

51
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,340
B-but...

52
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,840
There's no need to be shy.

53
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:15,080
Even if the first step is small,
it's a great step carved into our history.

54
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,920
Looks like Ryo-chan already carved it in.

55
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:21,480
It's really roomy in here.
It could fit ten people.

56
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:23,560
I'm coming too!

57
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,540
Forget it, this car is for two people only.

58
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:27,240
But it's so spacious!

59
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:32,140
That's why super-poor folks are rich: they
use all this space with just two people.

60
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,800
If you really insist on riding in it...

61
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:36,960
No way.

62
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:37,120
Tch!

63
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:41,840
Argh, damn it!
This is why I hate the old downtown!

64
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:45,680
That's because you were planning
to stick me in a car carrier.

65
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:48,220
Fine, I'll go in a different camper too.

66
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:51,420
Reiko, keep her company since she's pitiful.

67
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,580
You can build a camper at
Nakagawa's place, right?

68
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:57,860
Yes, Nakagawa Motors does
take custom orders, but

69
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,280
Alright, let's go with that.

70
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:02,600
Chief, let's all go next holiday!

71
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,920
Hohoho, not a bad idea for Ryotsu.

72
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:07,780
Camping sounds nice.

73
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:08,640
Senpai.

74
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,540
That's why, you see.

75
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,380
What?

76
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,320
Sorry, sorry.

77
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,420
Guess I'm a bit late.

78
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,120
Well, what do you think?

79
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:23,300
It's the fastest camper in the world,
built on a Ferrari!

80
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,020
Impressed?

81
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,640
Wow, this is something else.

82
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:26,460
It's pretty flashy, isn't it.

83
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,760
Ha it's brand-new, fresh off the line!

84
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:31,440
He really hates to lose, doesn't he.

85
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:35,140
Well, let's ignore the idiot and get going.

86
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:36,540
But...

87
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:40,520
Don't worry, we've already decided where we're going.
Let's meet up over there.

88
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,340
Now, Reiko, this way, please.

89
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:45,080
You're not driving?

90
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:48,680
Of course not! How can you savor
your wine properly if you're driving?

91
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:52,460
Please take your seats and fasten your seatbelts.
We're departing.

92
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,600
Step on it and really floor it!

93
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,780
Are the side mirrors just for decoration?

94
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,900
It's fine, there's a monitor inside.

95
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,440
The Porsche is starting to move!

96
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,580
What horsepower!

97
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,560
I got the oil spinning.

98
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,960
When did he get so good at driving?

99
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:19,560
We can't just sit here like this!

100
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:21,480
Chief, Terai, get in.

101
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:24,980
Don't fall behind, Nakagawa! Let's go!

102
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:25,820
Y-yes!

103
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,180
I'm not losing!

104
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,800
What a relief.

105
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:36,280
So this time you hired
a professional driver.

106
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:37,780
That's the wiser choice.

107
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,800
I told you so.

108
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,680
It's so I can enjoy some
wine slowly with Reiko.

109
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:46,940
A toast to your eyes.

110
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,680
A Ferrari is closing in!

111
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:54,620
What? Whatever you do, don't let him pass!

112
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,400
As expected of the Diablo!

113
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:59,520
The cars around us look
like they're standing still!

114
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,500
What, we're being passed by a camper van?

115
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,500
Am I seeing things?

116
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,720
It feels like the Porsche and
the Ferrari just overtook us.

117
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,820
This is awful.

118
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,280
Hey, faster!

119
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:19,660
With this shape, I've reached my limit.

120
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:22,580
That bastard's using a professional driver,
the cheat.

121
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:23,760
Nakagawa, don't swerve!

122
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,760
We're taking the crosswind head-on.

123
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,280
I can't go any further than this.

124
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,200
Damn it!

125
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,160
We don't need a break!

126
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,620
Then don't do it!

127
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:32,500
Quiet down!

128
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,620
Damn it! We got passed!

129
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,500
Passed? Well, I guess you could say that...

130
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:49,340
A swan! Switch it to twin
engines at the next drive-in!

131
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:54,040
What? This isn't a prank call!
I'm the vice president of Swan Railway!

132
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,020
Ugh! Come on, you lot!

133
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,820
Just do what you're told!

134
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:01,220
I'll pay any amount of money!

135
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:13,860
Pay up!

136
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,340
Senpai, the Porsche is catching up.

137
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,040
What?

138
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:27,080
Nakagawa, speed up!

139
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,480
The accelerator's been
floored this whole time.

140
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,000
What?

141
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:34,460
Looks like they swapped the engine.

142
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:37,940
Ugh, that graffiti on the back of
their car is really getting on my nerves.

143
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:41,100
Right, we're swapping our engine too.

144
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,000
We're practically at the campsite now.

145
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,900
What's the point of camping
if we lost to a Porsche?

146
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:47,940
I don't want to race a camper like this.

147
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:49,980
There must be a Servo Stick somewhere.

148
00:08:49,980 --> 00:08:50,560
There isn't.

149
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:54,340
Chief, they're getting away from us!

150
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:59,840
What, do we have to pay an entrance fee?

151
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,800
It's Chiratori's Porsche!

152
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,720
Pull up right in front of his face!

153
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,560
Yesss!

154
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,840
What are you doing?

155
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,680
Senpai, that's dangerous!

156
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:14,920
Ryo-chan!

157
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,120
Bakabon's -

158
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,340
Ryo-san!

159
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:18,660
Shut up!

160
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,540
We've arrived at the auto campground.

161
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:24,640
Camp... aaaaaah!

162
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,780
What? It's full of camper vans!

163
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:32,860
It's so crowded,
it's like a beach in summer break!

164
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:39,480
Convenience store, restaurant,
coin laundry, camping gear rentals, arcade,

165
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:44,080
video rentals,
and they even rent out decks and BS TVs!

166
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:48,240
They even have a lighter station! It's more
serious than those baseball fields over there.

167
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,660
Look, it's a designer brand store!

168
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:52,320
It's like a duty-free shop.

169
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:55,360
They've got everything here, haven't they.

170
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:58,740
At this rate,
I don't really feel like we've come camping.

171
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:03,280
Alright, let's go deeper into the mountains!

172
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,780
Camping only counts once
you're out in nature.

173
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:08,060
Exactly.

174
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:12,900
A camper only shows its
true worth out in nature.

175
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:17,000
Shiratori, for once we actually agree.

176
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,740
Dates are more fun where there are no clocks,
you know.

177
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:23,360
How dirty! So that was your ulterior motive!

178
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:30,500
As expected of the Simple Coat!
The Corsche engine is tough on rough roads!

179
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:34,300
A delicate Ferrari engine
could never handle this!

180
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:37,260
Senpai, we're biting into the ground!
We're going deeper into the mountains!

181
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,560
What are you biting for?!

182
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,900
Hey, hey, hey! You can handle this, right?!

183
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,260
I-I can't negotiate!

184
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:47,460
I won't lose to those
hundred-some super bastards!

185
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:50,208
G-give it back!

186
00:10:50,258 --> 00:10:53,440
Load it up! Loa-ad it up!

187
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:58,460
What do you think, Reiko?
This is nature at its finest

188
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:01,940
Yeah. But if I'm being honest,

189
00:11:01,990 --> 00:11:04,500
it feels more like nature's own menace.

190
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,940
Alright, we've arrived.
How about that? Nature at its finest!

191
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:15,160
Shiratori.
Coming to the same spot, what a coincidence.

192
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:16,720
Hmph, what a persistent guy.

193
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:27,280
Once we get here, first thing's cooking! Let's get right to it.
Senpai, since that group was a bit of a strong rival, let's take a little break first.

194
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:32,600
Fine, I suppose.
Then just for a little while, alright?

195
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:47,240
Right, the food's ready!

196
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,040
What? Ryotsu cooked?

197
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:53,680
Yeah, I offered to help,
but he insisted on making it alone.

198
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:55,560
Looks like curry.

199
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,700
I've got a bad feeling about this.

200
00:11:58,880 --> 00:11:59,640
Here you go!

201
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,560
This onion still has its outer skin on.

202
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,160
The carrots still have their leaves.

203
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:05,960
The potatoes still have their skins on, too.

204
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,100
What are you talking about?

205
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:09,880
To really enjoy nature,
you've got to keep the skins on.

206
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,420
That's what nature is all about.

207
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,020
Don't hold back, eat up.

208
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:14,280
I'd rather hold back.

209
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:15,900
Me too.

210
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:18,320
Senpai, these potatoes have eyes.

211
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:27,840
Out in nature, French cuisine
is the only way to go, isn't it?

212
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,680
Hey, this is the best setting ever, right?

213
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,960
No way,
he even got the chef to feel sorry for us...

214
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:36,680
Damn it!

215
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:41,897
How about you guys? I'm super rich, so

216
00:12:41,947 --> 00:12:43,300
I'm big-hearted!

217
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:47,140
W-what are you talking about?!
Camping always means curry!

218
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:50,760
French food?
Just being alive is a luxury, after all.

219
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:51,140
How fancy!

220
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,160
Well, my stomach doesn't lie.

221
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:55,380
Damn it, you traitor!

222
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:02,200
Music really is the best for an outdoor dinner,
isn't it?

223
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:11,160
Sorry to keep you waiting.

224
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:13,860
Songs follow the times,
and the times follow songs.

225
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:17,100
Kankichi Ryotsu will now perform
"The Sorrow of Men."

226
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,660
Karaoke with the great
outdoors as our backdrop.

227
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:23,940
This is the true pleasure of outdoor leisure,
a private moment all to ourselves.

228
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:34,540
Grinding local beans from scratch these days?
How super-broke can you get?

229
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,500
Ours has the latest, all genres.

230
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:40,720
It's laser karaoke covering everything
from the hit charts to summer songs.

231
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:43,580
Come on,
let's sing duets until morning, Reiko.

232
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,060
Do you have a song like this?

233
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:51,720
Then the 98, the X, or the 8000?

234
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,120
The 900?

235
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:00,440
After all, video games are the best.

236
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,840
If we're going to play,
let's go to the arcade.

237
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:09,760
Net team, begin the operation from Burida!

238
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:11,360
Net team, understood.

239
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,520
Movies are the best.

240
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:29,960
Be amazed, be amazed!

241
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:33,380
The ultimate one is still
the Electrical Parade!

242
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,120
What are you going on about?

243
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,260
Don't underestimate movies watched outdoors!

244
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:40,520
It'll be too bright to see anything.

245
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:43,600
Looks like the match is settled.

246
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,200
Damn it!

247
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:47,860
Boosting the output!

248
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,400
What?

249
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,700
Giving it 120% of everything!

250
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:55,980
How about that?

251
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:57,380
Nanaaa!

252
00:14:58,340 --> 00:14:59,060
Not yet, not yet.

253
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:00,660
Nana, how about this?

254
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,760
What on earth happened?

255
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:10,020
The engine won't start.

256
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:11,400
Looks like the battery died.

257
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:13,580
Can't we call for help?

258
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,400
My cell phone has no signal.

259
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,520
We're stuck, then.

260
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,000
Do something about it, Ryotsu!

261
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,520
The sky's starting to look suspicious.

262
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,160
Is it going to rain or something?

263
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:34,080
Well, playing cards by
candlelight isn't so bad either.

264
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,760
It's rather charming, isn't it.

265
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:37,680
Shiratori, why are you over here?

266
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:40,320
Super-poor people like you wouldn't
care about that sort of thing, right?

267
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,300
I care, you idiot!

268
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:42,960
The rain isn't stopping, is it.

269
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,080
It'd be scary if lightning struck us.

270
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:47,120
It's the mountain weather, after all.

271
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:53,460
Well, I hear there's plenty of
natural electricity to spare.

272
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,620
Diros, go out there and recharge it.

273
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:56,800
There's no way I can do that.

274
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:02,740
Aaaaaaah!

275
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:10,220
Aaaaaaah!

276
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:12,400
Aaaaaaah!

277
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,180
Aaaaaaah!

278
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:16,400
Aaaaaaah!

279
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:16,480
Aaaaaaah!

280
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:16,520
Aaaaaaah!

281
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:16,700
Aaaaaaah!

282
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:17,180
Aaaaaaah!

283
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:17,220
Aaaaaaah!

284
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:17,480
Aaaaaah!

285
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:17,500
Aaaaaah!

286
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,820
Worry about the people inside the car,
not the car itself!

287
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:21,580
The people inside are fine, though.

288
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:23,440
After all, he's a super-rich guy.

289
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,280
Without knowing it,
it's Reiji's custom camper.

290
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,340
There's nothing coming
from the other side, though.

291
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:29,680
Light-type airbags?

292
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:32,500
I bet the inside has those too, right?

293
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,960
Well, of course it has them, but...

294
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,660
So they're the light type?

295
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:48,180
We need to find somewhere to take shelter,
it's dangerous.

296
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,800
There's a cave on the other
side of the suspension bridge.

297
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,780
Saved!

298
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,540
That's quite an old suspension bridge.

299
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:58,800
This bridge is rotten.

300
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:00,480
Please be careful.

301
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:03,300
If we don't cross quickly,
this bridge might collapse.

302
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,340
It might fall, you know.

303
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:08,420
Then I'll pay you money.

304
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:12,620
Alright, now let me go first.

305
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:16,540
No, that won't do, stop!

306
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,520
Senpai, that's dangerous!
What are you doing?

307
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:30,660
Did they... is Senpai done for?

308
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:34,600
Hey, don't kill me off on your own!
Hurry up and pull me back up!

309
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,800
Because I'll be the one paying.

310
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:37,860
What should we do?

311
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,580
Everything I say out loud
ends up coming true...

312
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:42,940
It's a coincidence.

313
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:45,260
If it's bothering you,
try saying something with a positive spin.

314
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:50,480
Nobody knows we're camping way
out in the mountains like this,

315
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,780
and even if help comes,
there's a risk of a secondary disaster...

316
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:56,400
Where's the positive thinking in that?

317
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:01,920
But it's cold, I'm getting hungry,
and I can't think of anything fun.

318
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:05,000
How about a barbecue party around a bonfire?
That'd be pretty good.

319
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,220
I'll pay for it.
Someone go buy the ingredients!

320
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:13,940
I'm so hungry.

321
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:16,460
Hold it in. If you say it out loud,
I'll be even less inclined to share.

322
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:21,020
Canned food, of all things,
out here, and two of them.

323
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:22,680
Well done, Ryotsu!

324
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,940
Ryo-san, you're amazing, senpai!

325
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:25,760
Ryo-chan, you're the best!

326
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:28,860
Now, I'll savor these all by myself.

327
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:34,560
Hey, you guys are something else. Well, you
are my juniors, but isn't that a bit harsh?

328
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:42,440
Yeah, it's harsh. Which is it? You
betrayed the curry I made with all my heart.

329
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:49,000
You chose Shiwatori's French cuisine over that curry.
I'm not giving these cans to people like you.

330
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:52,660
Delicious.

331
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:56,160
This isn't the time for such meanness,
Ryo-chan.

332
00:18:56,160 --> 00:19:02,080
That's right. Let bygones be bygones. Even just a tiny bit will do,
so please share with everyone, senpai.

333
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,980
No way. I'm getting quite full.

334
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:09,040
Well, there's no help for it,
I guess I'll eat the second one too.

335
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:14,580
Now, how should I eat this one?

336
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:15,780
Ryo-chan

337
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:19,700
Hey, Shiratori, Reiko's going hungry!

338
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,000
How much will you pay per fish?

339
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,100
There are twenty little sardines in the can.

340
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:27,060
Even at 1,000 yen each, that's 20,000 yen.

341
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:30,360
Making a killing on a 350-yen can!

342
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,760
Alright, I'll buy it. One million yen okay?

343
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,360
Sold! One million yen.

344
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:43,040
Well, Reiko-san, this super-rich Reiji
Shiratori has reserved the canned food.

345
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:44,460
Just the two of us

346
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:45,600
Shiratori-san

347
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:46,480
Thank you

348
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,120
I won't forget this kindness.

349
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:48,760
Thank you very much.

350
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,000
Well, of course.

351
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:04,700
Come on, everyone,
let's eat modestly, shall we?

352
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:06,900
Did you hear that?

353
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:09,400
Where did Ryo-san go?

354
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:10,840
Exactly.

355
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:11,440
Ryo-chan

356
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,240
At this early hour,

357
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:46,460
Anything will do!
Just give me something to get me home!

358
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:08,020
Well done, Ryotsu!

359
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:12,400
Going out to buy food for everyone,
as expected of you!

360
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,140
You're a model police officer.

361
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,080
So help is on its way, then, right?

362
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:18,000
Hah.

363
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:21,680
Wait, you didn't call anyone?

364
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:24,680
No way, you went all the way to the shop
at the foot of the mountain and didn't...

365
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,720
Shut up, I didn't call anyone.

366
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,840
Hah.

367
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:31,660
Alright, with this many supplies,
we'll be fine for a month or two.

368
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:32,860
Hah.

369
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,920
Somehow, all the shine just went out of you.

370
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:38,700
Well, I suppose we'll just take
Ryo-san's kindness and run with it.

371
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:41,580
Idiot, do you intend to repay
someone's effort with mere kindness?

372
00:21:43,580 --> 00:21:46,760
So, the wonderful goods
here are all for sale.

373
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:50,760
Step right up! Whoever wants them can bid.
This is true democracy!

374
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:56,440
First up, this washbasin and towel. Right now,
I'll throw in this toothbrush set too!

375
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:59,520
I want it, but it's expensive, isn't it?

376
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:03,000
Don't worry, I'll buy it.
Is one million yen okay?

377
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,560
If nobody else is buying, that's fine.

378
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:09,180
But water is sold separately.
Maybe two million yen a bottle.

379
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:13,760
Fine, I'll buy it for three million yen a bottle.
Give me three.

380
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:15,980
There you go, there you go.

381
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:20,100
You call it an auction, senpai, but you're
setting the prices yourself, aren't you?

382
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:21,920
Your target is painfully obvious.

383
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:24,640
Hiratori, who doesn't even notice,
is a Shiratori too.

384
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:27,380
How about five million for
that milk and bread over there?

385
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:28,180
Shut up!

386
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:31,720
One roll of toilet paper,
maybe ten million yen.

387
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:36,100
Cheap, cheap!
Thirty million sounds about right.

388
00:22:36,580 --> 00:22:38,880
Cup noodles for lunch, fifty million!

389
00:22:39,180 --> 00:22:40,720
I'll lend you the 3 o'clock snack!

390
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:41,620
One hundred million!

391
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:45,660
Ryo-san, he's planning to squeeze
every last yen out of Shiratori.

392
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:47,580
You two are as bad as each other.

393
00:22:47,580 --> 00:22:50,320
How twisted can those two get?

394
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:50,920
That's it!

395
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:00,360
Saved!

396
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,720
Now we can go home.

397
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:04,080
This is all the cash we have on hand!

398
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,460
With this,
let's take that soy sauce and miso.

399
00:23:09,180 --> 00:23:11,960
Without cash,
we can't sell you the rest of the goods.

400
00:23:16,020 --> 00:23:18,000
Chief, what should we do about those two?

401
00:23:20,620 --> 00:23:22,840
With that much food, they'll be fine, right?

402
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:24,620
Just leave them as they are for a while.

403
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,660
Isn't that a bit pitiful?

404
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:31,620
Come on. If that keeps Japan's peace intact,

405
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:33,140
those two should be happy with that, right?

406
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:37,440
That caramel

407
00:23:39,180 --> 00:23:40,260
How about a gold card?

408
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:41,420
Fine by me, Garo.

409
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:43,760
Then I'll appraise it at 300 million yen.

410
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:47,280
That chocolate is Buzzer's platinum card.

411
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,240
Alright, 500 million.

412
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:51,640
The potato chips are Orca's hyper card.

413
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,440
Alright, 1 billion.

414
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:54,480
And then...

415
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:55,960
Still, still, still...

416
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,100
I'll throw this in too.

417
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,600
That's still only 100 million.

418
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:07,380
What's all this Jaguar nonsense?

419
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:08,320
Good time.

420
00:24:09,180 --> 00:24:11,060
Japanese through and through, yet you
went and got all wrapped up in Britain!

421
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:14,640
And on top of that, he's a super sore
loser who never admits his own mistakes.

422
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:17,700
What? A duel? Fine, I'll take you on!

423
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:20,600
Next time: the outrageous Professor appears!

424
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:21,620
Nice to meet you.

425
00:24:39,180 --> 00:24:43,200
I want to do a mountain of things.

426
00:24:45,180 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

427
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:59,200
I want to be freer than a bird.

428
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:07,120
At the speed of a kaleidoscope,
a lady's dreams keep changing.

429
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:15,060
Heart of love, sorry, I give in.

430
00:25:15,060 --> 00:25:22,220
The dazzle of living
the panoramic future live.

431
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:30,120
You understand, right?
Sorry, just wait for me.

